* With their loss to Penrith, the Melbourne Storm missed the finals with a losing record for the first time since 2002, the first of coach Craig Bellamy's 24 year career.{{efn|The Melbourne Storm also missed the finals in 2010, when the club was penalised for [[Melbourne Storm salary cap breach|salary cap breaches]] and received the wooden spoon; the club would have otherwise finished fifth on the ladder that year.}}<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-20/nrl-live-melbourne-storm-penrith-panthers/107060788|title=Penrith Panthers end Melbourne Storm's slim NRL finals hopes with 22-14 win|publisher=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] ([[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]])|first=Jon|last=Healy|date=20 August 2026|accessdate=21 August 2026}}</ref> It was also the first time both reigning Grand Finalists missed out on the finals the following year since [[2006 NRL season|2006]].
* Penrith won in Melbourne at AAMI Park for the first time since [[2018 NRL season results#round 25|round 25, 2018]].

